      "id": "exam/edexcel-8ma0-01-2020-october/q1",
      "question": "<p>A curve has equation</p><div class=\"equation\" data-math=\"y = 2x^3 - 4x + 5\" data-display=\"true\"></div><p>Find the equation of the tangent to the curve at the point <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"P(2, 13)\"></span>.</p><p>Write your answer in the form <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"y = mx + c\"></span>, where <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"m\"></span> and <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"c\"></span> are integers to be found.</p><p>Solutions relying on calculator technology are not acceptable.</p><p><span class=\"marks\">(5)</span></p>",
