    {
      "id": "exam/edexcel-8ma0-01-2020-october/q2",
      "question": "<p>[In this question the unit vectors <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"\\mathbf i\"></span> and <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"\\mathbf j\"></span> are due east and due north respectively.]</p><p>A coastguard station <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"O\"></span> monitors the movements of a small boat.</p><p>At 10:00 the boat is at the point <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"(4\\mathbf i - 2\\mathbf j)\"></span> km relative to <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"O\"></span>.</p><p>At 12:45 the boat is at the point <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"(-3\\mathbf i - 5\\mathbf j)\"></span> km relative to <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"O\"></span>.</p><p>The motion of the boat is modelled as that of a particle moving in a straight line at constant speed.</p><p>(a) Calculate the bearing on which the boat is moving, giving your answer in degrees to one decimal place.</p><p><span class=\"marks\">(3)</span></p><p>(b) Calculate the speed of the boat, giving your answer in <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"\\mathrm{km}\\,\\mathrm{h}^{-1}\"></span></p><p><span class=\"marks\">(3)</span></p>",
