    {
      "id": "exam/edexcel-8ma0-01-2020-october/q4",
      "question": "<p>In 1997 the average CO<span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"_2\"></span> emissions of new cars in the UK was 190 g/km.</p><p>In 2005 the average CO<span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"_2\"></span> emissions of new cars in the UK had fallen to 169 g/km.</p><p>Given <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"A\"></span> g/km is the average CO<span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"_2\"></span> emissions of new cars in the UK <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"n\"></span> years after 1997 and using a linear model,</p><p>(a) form an equation linking <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"A\"></span> with <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"n\"></span>.</p><p><span class=\"marks\">(3)</span></p><p>In 2016 the average CO<span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"_2\"></span> emissions of new cars in the UK was 120 g/km.</p><p>(b) Comment on the suitability of your model in light of this information.</p><p><span class=\"marks\">(3)</span></p>",
