      "id": "exam/edexcel-8ma0-01-2020-october/q5",
      "question": "<figure class=\"practice-figure\" style=\"max-width:132mm;margin:2mm auto\"><img src=\"resources/exams/edexcel-8ma0-01-2020-october/q05-figure.svg\" alt=\"Figure 1. Roof support with four steel beams and the marked 27 degree angle.\"></figure><p>Figure 1 shows the design for a structure used to support a roof.</p><p>The structure consists of four steel beams, <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"AB\"></span>, <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"BD\"></span>, <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"BC\"></span> and <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"AD\"></span>.</p><p>Given <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"AB = 12\\text{ m}\"></span>, <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"BC = BD = 7\\text{ m}\"></span> and angle <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"BAC = 27^\\circ\"></span></p><p>(a) find, to one decimal place, the size of angle <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"ACB\"></span>.</p><p><span class=\"marks\">(3)</span></p><p>The steel beams can only be bought in whole metre lengths.</p><p>(b) Find the minimum length of steel that needs to be bought to make the complete structure.</p><p><span class=\"marks\">(3)</span></p>",
