      "question": "<p>Given that <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"k\"></span> is a positive constant and <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"\\int_{1}^{k} \\left( \\frac{5}{2\\sqrt{x}} + 3 \\right) \\mathrm{d}x = 4\"></span></p><p>(a) show that <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"3k + 5\\sqrt{k} - 12 = 0\"></span></p><p><span class=\"marks\">(4)</span></p><p>(b) Hence, using algebra, find any values of <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"k\"></span> such that</p><div class=\"equation\" data-math=\"\\int_{1}^{k} \\left( \\frac{5}{2\\sqrt{x}} + 3 \\right) \\mathrm{d}x = 4\" data-display=\"true\"></div><p><span class=\"marks\">(4)</span></p>",
