    {
      "id": "exam/edexcel-8ma0-01-2020-october/q8",
      "question": "<p>The temperature, <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"\\theta^{\\circ}\\text{C}\"></span>, of a cup of tea <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"t\"></span> minutes after it was placed on a table in a room, is modelled by the equation</p><div class=\"equation\" data-math=\"\\theta = 18 + 65e^{-\\frac{t}{8}} \\quad t \\geqslant 0\" data-display=\"true\"></div><p>Find, according to the model,</p><p>(a) the temperature of the cup of tea when it was placed on the table,</p><p><span class=\"marks\">(1)</span></p><p>(b) the value of <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"t\"></span>, to one decimal place, when the temperature of the cup of tea was <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"35^{\\circ}\\text{C}\"></span>.</p><p><span class=\"marks\">(3)</span></p><p>(c) Explain why, according to this model, the temperature of the cup of tea could not fall to <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"15^{\\circ}\\text{C}\"></span>.</p><p><span class=\"marks\">(1)</span></p><figure class=\"practice-figure\" style=\"max-width:108mm;margin:2mm auto\"><img src=\"resources/exams/edexcel-8ma0-01-2020-october/q08-figure.svg\" alt=\"Figure 2. Temperature curve with points (0, 94) and (8, 50), and asymptote l.\"></figure><p>The temperature, <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"\\mu^{\\circ}\\text{C}\"></span>, of a second cup of tea <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"t\"></span> minutes after it was placed on a table in a different room, is modelled by the equation</p><div class=\"equation\" data-math=\"\\mu = A + Be^{-\\frac{t}{8}} \\quad t \\geqslant 0\" data-display=\"true\"></div><p>where <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"A\"></span> and <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"B\"></span> are constants.</p><p>Figure 2 shows a sketch of <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"\\mu\"></span> against <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"t\"></span> with two data points that lie on the curve.</p><p>The line <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"l\"></span>, also shown on Figure 2, is the asymptote to the curve.</p><p>Using the equation of this model and the information given in Figure 2</p><p>(d) find an equation for the asymptote <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"l\"></span>.</p><p><span class=\"marks\">(4)</span></p>",
      "steps": [
