      "id": "exam/edexcel-8ma0-01-2020-october/q9",
      "question": "<figure class=\"practice-figure\" style=\"max-width:132mm;margin:2mm auto\"><img src=\"resources/exams/edexcel-8ma0-01-2020-october/q09-figure.svg\" alt=\"Figure 3. Cosine curve with the marked minimum P.\"></figure><p>Figure 3 shows part of the curve with equation <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"y = 3 \\cos x^\\circ\"></span>.</p><p>The point <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"P(c, d)\"></span> is a minimum point on the curve with <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"c\"></span> being the smallest negative value of <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"x\"></span> at which a minimum occurs.</p><p>(a) State the value of <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"c\"></span> and the value of <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"d\"></span>.</p><p><span class=\"marks\">(1)</span></p><p>(b) State the coordinates of the point to which <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"P\"></span> is mapped by the transformation which transforms the curve with equation <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"y = 3 \\cos x^\\circ\"></span> to the curve with equation</p><p>(i) <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"y = 3 \\cos \\left( \\frac{x^\\circ}{4} \\right)\"></span></p><p>(ii) <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"y = 3 \\cos (x - 36)^\\circ\"></span></p><p><span class=\"marks\">(2)</span></p><p>(c) Solve, for <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"450^\\circ \\leq \\theta &lt; 720^\\circ\"></span>,</p><div class=\"equation\" data-math=\"3 \\cos \\theta = 8 \\tan \\theta\" data-display=\"true\"></div><p>giving your solution to one decimal place.</p><p>In part (c) you must show all stages of your working.</p><p>Solutions relying entirely on calculator technology are not acceptable.</p><p><span class=\"marks\">(5)</span></p>",
