      "id": "exam/edexcel-8ma0-01-2020-october/q10",
      "question": "<p><span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"g(x) = 2x^3 + x^2 - 41x - 70\"></span></p><p>(a) Use the factor theorem to show that <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"g(x)\"></span> is divisible by <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"(x - 5)\"></span>.</p><p><span class=\"marks\">(2)</span></p><p>(b) Hence, showing all your working, write <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"g(x)\"></span> as a product of three linear factors.</p><p><span class=\"marks\">(4)</span></p><p>The finite region <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"R\"></span> is bounded by the curve with equation <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"y = g(x)\"></span> and the <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"x\"></span>-axis, and lies below the <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"x\"></span>-axis.</p><p>(c) Find, using algebraic integration, the exact value of the area of <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"R\"></span>.</p><p><span class=\"marks\">(4)</span></p>",
