      "question": "<p>(i) A circle <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"C_1\"></span> has equation</p><div class=\"equation\" data-math=\"x^2 + y^2 + 18x - 2y + 30 = 0\" data-display=\"true\"></div><p>The line <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"l\"></span> is the tangent to <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"C_1\"></span> at the point <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"P(-5, 7)\"></span>.</p><p>Find an equation of <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"l\"></span> in the form <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"ax + by + c = 0\"></span>, where <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"a, b\"></span> and <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"c\"></span> are integers to be found.</p><p><span class=\"marks\">(5)</span></p><p>(ii) A different circle <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"C_2\"></span> has equation</p><div class=\"equation\" data-math=\"x^2 + y^2 - 8x + 12y + k = 0\" data-display=\"true\"></div><p>where <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"k\"></span> is a constant.</p><p>Given that <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"C_2\"></span> lies entirely in the 4th quadrant, find the range of possible values for <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"k\"></span>.</p><p><span class=\"marks\">(4)</span></p>",
