      "id": "exam/edexcel-8ma0-01-2020-october/q12",
      "question": "<p>An advertising agency is monitoring the number of views of an online advert.</p><p>The equation</p><div class=\"equation\" data-math=\"\\log_{10} V = 0.072t + 2.379 \\quad 1 \\leq t \\leq 30, t \\in \\mathbb{N}\" data-display=\"true\"></div><p>is used to model the total number of views of the advert, <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"V\"></span>, in the first <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"t\"></span> days after the advert went live.</p><p>(a) Show that <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"V = ab^t\"></span> where <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"a\"></span> and <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"b\"></span> are constants to be found.</p><p>Give the value of <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"a\"></span> to the nearest whole number and give the value of <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"b\"></span> to 3 significant figures.</p><p><span class=\"marks\">(4)</span></p><p>(b) Interpret, with reference to the model, the value of <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"ab\"></span>.</p><p><span class=\"marks\">(1)</span></p><p>Using this model, calculate</p><p>(c) the total number of views of the advert in the first 20 days after the advert went live.</p><p>Give your answer to 2 significant figures.</p><p><span class=\"marks\">(2)</span></p>",
